{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfweGcfAARbswi2kZPfH7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or waited for the rule to run, so I haven't confirmed the panels render or that the rule fires.\n\n**Data:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` has web-traffic fields:\n- Request details: `timestamp`, `clientip`, `request`, `url`, `extension`, `bytes`, `host`, `referer`\n- Client and origin: `agent`, `machine.os`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`\n- Response code: `response`, which is a string, so I filter on `response.keyword`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-f5322180 Web logs overview\" has five panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by extension\n- Top source countries\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-f5322180-web-logs-overview-cffaf103ddff.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-f5322180 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule.\n- **Schedule:** It checks every minute.\n- **Condition:** It fires when more than 10 documents match `response.keyword: 5*` within the last 5 minutes.\n- **Created disabled:** It was created disabled and I enabled it afterwards. Its ID is `6fb98cdc-315c-4103-9bd2-9e1bb77ac3b9`.\n- **No action attached:** I didn't attach a notification action, so a firing will only show in Kibana's alerts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":21294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169},"output_tokens":523,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"72cf7f1e-76fe-4477-b06e-d5f9874b8a4e","timestamp"